# fixedbugs, defect 555, lane b18-ffi, 2026-10-10 (panel 202's C1; the
# sitting's `fp`), the shape beside the repair.
#
# Two modules bind `twice` from two headers each defining it `static
# inline`, of `int` here and of `long long` in the other. A `static`
# definition is its unit's own, so the two never meet at the link, and the
# question of two declarations of one name passes them over: the program
# builds and prints each module's value, as it did before the repair.
use fixedbugs555/static_long

extern "fixedbugs-555-static-int.h"
    function twice(x: i32) -> i32

function main()
    print(static_long.doubled(x: 3))
    print(twice(x: 4))
